Track 3: Noctu-Grammaton
- Story & Context: Legends swelled around the station's final, garbled message, dubbed the "Noctu-Grammaton," a sonic palimpsest believed to contain instructions for navigating the coming storms, though few truly understood its fragmented warnings, and its last faint broadcast, laced with an unsettling guttural hum that could vibrate bone, was said to have permanently altered the local weather patterns, leaving a pervasive low-pressure system over the region, a permanent monument to its power. "They say it's etched into the very sky, a signal for the unseen."
